## Why This Is Asked

This question tests depth in CAPA design for cross-tenant data exposure caused by policy migration bugs in a real-time data mesh. It evaluates the ability to model evidence, define a region-aware lifecycle, implement a minimal API, and build measurable containment strategies plus RCA artifacts and canary rollouts.

## Key Concepts

- CAPA data model capturing evidence, tenant IDs, policy metadata, dashboards, and timestamps
- Region-aware lifecycle state machine for CAPA progression
- RBAC/policy migration risks in real-time data platforms
- Minimal REST API design to link logs/traces to CAPA records
- Canary rollout and region-validated testing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal CAPA creation endpoint
app.post('/api/capa', async (req, res) => {
  const { incidentId, tenants, dashboards, policyHash, evidence } = req.body;
  // Persist CAPA, link logs/traces, trigger workflow
  res.status(201).send({ id: incidentId });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate cross-tenant exposure detection at scale across regions?
- What data retention and privacy considerations would you encode in the CAPA API?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a full CAPA program around a nuanced data-leak due to a race in schema evolution, ensuring cross-tenant and cross-region considerations are baked in.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model with evidence, tenant/stream IDs, redaction configs, logs, RCA link
- Region-aware lifecycle: detect, contain, remediate, verify, close
- Minimal REST API for CAPA creation/update with linked artifacts
- Cross-tenant/region metrics: recurrence, MTTR, false positives; canary rollout
- RCA template and validation workflow

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example CAPA data model (TypeScript)
type CAPA = {
  id: string;
  tenantId: string;
  streamId: string;
  evidenceUri: string;
  redactionConfigId: string;
  status: 'detected'|'contained'|'remediated'|'verified'|'closed';
  region: string;
  createdAt: string;
  linkedLogs?: string[];
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you integrate with existing incident management and alerting tooling?
- How would you design canary validation across regions to prevent regression?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests CAPA fundamentals under real-world data issues: region awareness, basic data modeling, and a simple remediation flow.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model, lifecycle, REST API, regional metrics, RCA, canary.
- Trade-offs: latency of detection vs noise, data retention for evidence.

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal Express REST endpoints
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
app.use(express.json());
let store = [];
app.post('/caps', (req, res)=>{ const cap={id:Date.now().toString(), ...req.body, status:'detected', created_at:new Date().toISOString()}; store.push(cap); res.status(201).json(cap);});
app.put('/caps/:id', (req,res)=>{ const idx=store.findIndex(c=>c.id===req.params.id); if(idx>=0){store[idx]={...store[idx], ...req.body}; res.json(store[idx]);} else res.status(404).end();});
app.listen(3000);
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate and test the canary plan before broader rollout?
- What telemetry would you capture to ensure no regression after remediation?
